cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NuMatRx, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "NuMatRx: a matrix burnup framework for reactor physics and stellar nucleosynthesis"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/rspassyuk/NuMatRx"
abstract: >-
  NuMatRx is a Python framework with a graphical interface for nuclear reaction
  networks. It reads evaluated nuclear data (ENDF-6 libraries, MACS tables,
  TALYS output and a user database), builds transmutation networks on an
  interactive isotope chart, and solves the burnup equations with
  matrix-exponential methods (CRAM-16, adaptive CRAM-16, CRAM-48, Padé).
  It provides heat release, equilibrium search, cycle analysis, one-at-a-time
  sensitivity, and time and neutron-exposure averaging of abundances, for
  reactor physics and s-process nucleosynthesis studies.
keywords:
  - nuclear reaction networks
  - burnup
  - matrix exponential
  - CRAM
  - s-process
  - nucleosynthesis
  - ENDF
